import mundane theorem    stdlib/sums/sum-extended
import mundane theorem    stdlib/sums/sum-single

theorem shifted-pronic-sum
  note        By induction on n: adding (k + 1)(k + 3) to k(k + 1)(2k + 7)/6
              gives (k + 1)(k + 2)(2k + 9)/6.
  let n ∈ ℕ                                                           (H1)
  then Σ(k = 1 to n) k·(k + 2) = n·(n + 1)·(2n + 7)/6

let S(m) = Σ(j = 1 to m) j·(j + 2), for m ∈ ℕ                         (D1)
       reads the sum of the first m products j·(j + 2)

1.  For all k ∈ ℕ, S(k) = k·(k + 1)·(2k + 7)/6.
    induction on k starting at 1

    base
    1.1.  Σ(j = 1 to 1) j·(j + 2) = 1·(1 + 2)
          mun:sum-single a := 1

    1.2.  S(1) = 1·(1 + 1)·(2·1 + 7)/6
          calculation
            S(1) = Σ(j = 1 to 1) j·(j + 2)       D1
                 = 1·(1 + 2)                     1.1
                 = 1·(1 + 1)·(2·1 + 7)/6         arithmetic

    step
    let k ∈ ℕ                                                         (K)
    assume step 1 is true for k, the induction hypothesis             (IH)

    1.3.  Σ(j = 1 to k + 1) j·(j + 2) = Σ(j = 1 to k) j·(j + 2) + (k + 1)·((k + 1) + 2)
          mun:sum-extended a := 1, n := k
          requires k ≥ 1: from K

    1.4.  S(k + 1) = S(k) + (k + 1)·((k + 1) + 2)
          calculation
            S(k + 1) = Σ(j = 1 to k + 1) j·(j + 2)                        D1
                     = Σ(j = 1 to k) j·(j + 2) + (k + 1)·((k + 1) + 2)    1.3
                     = S(k) + (k + 1)·((k + 1) + 2)                       D1

    1.5.  S(k) + (k + 1)·((k + 1) + 2) = k·(k + 1)·(2k + 7)/6 + (k + 1)·((k + 1) + 2)
          substitute S(k) = k·(k + 1)·(2k + 7)/6 (IH)

    1.6.  k·(k + 1)·(2k + 7)/6 + (k + 1)·((k + 1) + 2) = (k + 1)·((k + 1) + 1)·(2(k + 1) + 7)/6
          algebra

    1.7.  S(k + 1) = (k + 1)·((k + 1) + 1)·(2(k + 1) + 7)/6
          calculation
            S(k + 1) = S(k) + (k + 1)·((k + 1) + 2)                           1.4
                     = k·(k + 1)·(2k + 7)/6 + (k + 1)·((k + 1) + 2)           1.5
                     = (k + 1)·((k + 1) + 1)·(2(k + 1) + 7)/6                 1.6

2.  S(n) = n·(n + 1)·(2n + 7)/6
    instantiate k := n in line 1

3.  Σ(k = 1 to n) k·(k + 2) = n·(n + 1)·(2n + 7)/6
    calculation
      Σ(k = 1 to n) k·(k + 2) = S(n)                        D1
                              = n·(n + 1)·(2n + 7)/6        2
